# Namespaces

Namespaces are used to avoid name collisions between classes, functions, and constants. They allow you to group related code together.

```php
namespace MyProject\Utilities;
class Logger { ... }
```

# Error Handling

Modern PHP uses Exceptions for error handling. Use `try`, `catch`, and `finally` blocks to handle runtime errors gracefully.

```php
try {
    throw new Exception("Error!");
} catch (Exception $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage();
}
```

